 story  a disservice to not allow our viewers to  feel what the characters are feeling it  and the first half of the season really  did take us into some deep dark places  you know you see Daryl broken you see  Rick broken you're watching your heroes  ground into the dirt and it's a really  uncomfortable scenario to experience but  the second half of the season we get a  lot of Redemption and we see that Daryl  has escaped from the sanctuary and Rick  has decided to fight so everything that  we set up on the first half of the  season now our momentum is taking us  towards a much different place people  like yeah there's the Daryl I love  that's the Rick I love this is gonna be  great they're going to get back together  and kick some butt so also it's a  testament to Steven Yeun and Michael  Cudlitz for making those characters so  lovable that people freak out when  they're gone yeah and it's and it's  interesting for us to on the set you  know we've worked seven years with  Steven and in five years and you feel  that loss when they're gone  you know I mean I'm kind of I feel a  little responsible because I've killed  half of your characters on the show one  night I called Melissa McBride just to  say hello she's like what why you  calling me what's happening no I just  you worry you do yeah you  you're always anytime I call into the  back line  not like vehicle and I suppose lots of  people hoping that this will run on and  on there's a what rumors of an eighth  series in the pipeline some people  saying it could go as far as 12 series  because if the material in those comic  books how far you can push it how many  more people can you kill off well you  know it's a compelling story and that's  really what it's about when it's time to  run the story wraps up the story wraps  up but we have a lot of material to  cover and you know we have a lot of  great actors half of them that are from  here you're the only person it's not  from the UK literally kind of yeah right  